# Instructions

During your interaction with the user, if you find anything reusable in this project (e.g. version of a library, model name), especially about a fix to a mistake you made or a correction you received, you should take note in the `Lessons` section in the `general.mdc` file so you will not make the same mistake again. 

# Lessons

## User Specified Lessons
- Always use (activate) the virtual environment in ./.venv when executing python code. 
- If ./.venv does not exist, use uv to create one with python 3.13. 
- The `uv` package manager is available at `/home/cheng-yu/.local/bin/uv`.
- Always use `/home/cheng-yu/.local/bin/uv pip install` to install any new packages needed.
- LLM config uses **`LLM_BASE_URL`**, **`LLM_API_KEY`**, **`LLM_MODEL`** (no defaults). OpenAI-compatible **`chat/completions`**; AI Builders and OpenRouter are examples—set base URL accordingly.

## Cursor learned
- **Tavily / `POST /search/`** was removed from this project; discovery is **arXiv + RSS + optional newsroom** only. **`topic.json`** no longer has a `tavily` section.
- **arXiv** `export.arxiv.org` often returns **503**, **429**, or **slow reads**; `arxiv_client` sends a proper **User-Agent**, retries with **`Retry-After`** and long backoff for **429**; default read timeout **180s** (`ROM_NEWSLETTER_ARXIV_READ_TIMEOUT`); optional **`ROM_NEWSLETTER_ARXIV_USER_AGENT`** for CI; if it still fails, **`--no-arxiv`**.
- **Buttondown:** `rom-newsletter-buttondown` posts `dist/newsletter-<date>.html` with subject from JSON; needs **`BUTTONDOWN_API_KEY`**; uses **`status: about_to_send`** + **`X-Buttondown-Live-Dangerously: true`** for sends; **retries** 429/502/503/504 (API can return **503** + Heroku HTML). Weekly cron: `.github/workflows/weekly-newsletter.yml`. If JSON **`subject`** is empty, fallback is **`topic.json` → `buttondown.fallback_subject`** (built-in ROM default if no topic file).
- **Topic profile:** **`topic.json`** (or **`--topic`** / **`ROM_NEWSLETTER_TOPIC`**) holds arXiv Lucene body (**`arxiv: null`** skips API when sources still list arXiv), theme patterns / **`theme.disabled`**, compose fragments, section headings, Buttondown fallback. **`sources.json`** remains feeds/domains only.
- Compose **`subject`**: LLM must avoid **ROM/SciML Weekly**-style series labels and **lead with industry** when excerpts support it; user prompt lists **Industry** excerpts before **Research**.
- A `uv venv` environment may not have `.venv/bin/pip`; install packages with `/home/cheng-yu/.local/bin/uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python ...` (or `uv sync` if the project uses uv lock workflow).
- NVIDIA Newsroom RSS items often link to **external** domains (e.g. WSJ); RSS filtering should trust the **feed host** allowlist, not the article URL host.
- Page-date HTML parsing (e.g. newsroom article fetch) includes **`og:published_time`**, **JSON-LD** `datePublished`, and visible **English** dates (`March 17, 2026` / `17 March 2026`) after stripping `<!-- comments -->` (avoids Webflow “Last Published” in comments).
- Source config is **`sources.json` only** (no markdown list); `load_sources` expects JSON (`.json`/`.jsonc` or content starting with `{`). Default path is repo root (`--sources` overrides). Per-source **`rss`** and **`feed_hosts`** merge before built-in default RSS URLs in code; duplicate feed URLs dedupe with per-source entries winning.
- **`newsroom_listing: true`** uses built-in discovery in `newsroom_listings.py` for **`id`** `physicsx`, `neural-concept`, `emmi-ai`, **`siemens`** (en-us sitemap + `<lastmod>`), **`p1-ai`** (press URLs on `p-1.ai` homepage), **`luminary`** (Press cards on `luminary.ai/resources`), **`vinci4d`** (`getvinci.ai/news`), **`akselos`** (News-filter resource hub); complements per-source RSS the same way.
- Each **`SearchHit`** carries **`source_category`** from the source row’s **`category`** when the URL matches a source; compose splits **research** vs **industry** prompt bundles from that (arXiv API hits are always `papers`; unmatched hosts default to **industry**). **`source_category_for_url`** maps **`papers`** vs **`industry`** when a host matches a source row.
- RSS feeds on a hostname **not** listed among source domains need **`feed_hosts`** on that source entry in `sources.json` (e.g. `news.synopsys.com` for Synopsys feeds).
- Non-arXiv discovery hits are **theme-scored** (ROM/SciML/twins/CAE regexes) before compose; tune `--theme-min-score` / `--theme-backfill-min-score` if industry sections are noisy or too thin. **Physics AI** / **AI physics** in titles counts (newsroom hits often have title-only excerpts).
